592186045417] [17592186416354 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9de09353-fb9c-544f-8c67-c4ef2c4abd36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416355 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416355 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416355 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416355 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416355 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186416350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416355 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416355 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416355 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186416327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416355 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a54a21cb-93a2-537e-bb2f-71cc7631af9a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416357 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416357 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86853" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416357 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416357 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416357 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "15ea3713-dc0a-53ca-b70c-c22a6b79a105" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416357 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416358 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416358 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139474" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416358 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416358 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416358 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d93f91c3-07ee-5843-9236-38543eb4a92a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416358 #edb/ref 1074 "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{11}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2-0)^{2}+(6-0)^{2}+(2-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+36+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{44} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416360 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186416364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416360 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "22bcf45c-640c-575f-a16d-c7b5c8b62a7e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416360 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186416358 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416361 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186416363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416361 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6a574829-aeac-59dc-b7f2-f0730e2342d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416361 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186184778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416362 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186416361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416362 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a7cb447b-1a24-58bb-a8de-9b45b9c2e4bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416362 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186416359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416363 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186416360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416363 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c19427b8-35d1-5ec6-a82b-132f5b304d1b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416363 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186416357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416364 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e5babb95-1720-532d-87a1-a1a7b17c6c2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186416364 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186416356 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
